    "q-183378": {
      "dom_id": "questionContainer",
      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "Find the truth set of $P(x)⇔Q(x)$ given the following predicates defined over the universal set $R:$\n\n- $P(x):$ ${x}^{2}\\le 9$\n\n- $Q(x):$ $5x-3>7$",
      "worked_solution": "Since we have that\n\n$$\nP(x)⇔Q(x)≡(P(x)∧Q(x))∨(¬P(x)∧¬Q(x)),\n$$\n\n \n\nthe corresponding truth set can be found as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}_{P⇔Q}=({T}_{P}\\cap {T}_{Q})\\cup ({\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}\\cap {\\overset{―}{T}}_{Q})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we note the following:\n\n- To find the truth set of $P(x),$ we solve the inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & \\le 9 \\\\ -3 & \\le x\\le 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the truth set of $P(x)$ is \n${T}_{P}=[-3,3].$ \nAs a result, the complement is\n${\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}=(-\\infty ,-3)\\cup (3,\\infty ).$\n\n- To find the truth set of $Q(x),$ we solve the inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x-3 & >7 \\\\ 5x & >10 \\\\ x & >2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the truth set of $Q(x)$ is\n${T}_{Q}=(2,\\infty ),$\nand its complement is\n${\\overset{―}{T}}_{Q}=(-\\infty ,2].$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}_{P}\\cap {T}_{Q} & =[-3,3]\\cap (2,\\infty ) \\\\  & =(2,3] \\\\ {\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}\\cap {\\overset{―}{T}}_{Q} & =((-\\infty ,-3)\\cup (3,\\infty ))\\cap (-\\infty ,2] \\\\  & =(-\\infty ,-3) \\\\ {T}_{P⇔Q} & =({T}_{P}\\cap {T}_{Q})\\cup ({\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}\\cap {\\overset{―}{T}}_{Q}) \\\\  & =(2,3]\\cup (-\\infty ,-3) \\\\  & =(-\\infty ,-3)\\cup (2,3].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
